#: ../NEWS:11410
msgid ""
":gh:`115015`: Fix a bug in Argument Clinic that generated incorrect code for"
" methods with no parameters that use the :ref:`METH_METHOD | METH_FASTCALL |"
" METH_KEYWORDS <METH_METHOD-METH_FASTCALL-METH_KEYWORDS>` calling "
"convention. Only the positional parameter count was checked; any keyword "
"argument passed would be silently accepted."
msgstr ""
":gh:`115015`: 修复Argument Clinic中的一个bug，该bug会为没有参数但使用 :ref:`METH_METHOD | "
"METH_FASTCALL | METH_KEYWORDS <METH_METHOD-METH_FASTCALL-METH_KEYWORDS>` "
"调用约定的方法生成错误的代码。之前只检查了位置参数的数量；任何传递的关键字参数都会被静默接受。"

#: ../NEWS:11419
msgid ""
":gh:`111140`: Adds :c:func:`PyLong_AsNativeBytes`, "
":c:func:`PyLong_FromNativeBytes` and "
":c:func:`PyLong_FromUnsignedNativeBytes` functions."
msgstr ""
":gh:`111140`: 添加 "
":c:func:`PyLong_AsNativeBytes`、:c:func:`PyLong_FromNativeBytes` 和 "
":c:func:`PyLong_FromUnsignedNativeBytes` 函数。"

#: ../NEWS:11423
msgid ""
":gh:`114685`: :c:func:`PyBuffer_FillInfo` now raises a :exc:`SystemError` if"
" called with :c:macro:`PyBUF_READ` or :c:macro:`PyBUF_WRITE` as flags. These"
" flags should only be used with the ``PyMemoryView_*`` C API."
msgstr ""
":gh:`114685`: 如果 :c:func:`PyBuffer_FillInfo` 被调用时使用了 :c:macro:`PyBUF_READ` 或"
" :c:macro:`PyBUF_WRITE` 作为标志，现在会引发 "
":exc:`SystemError`。这些标志应仅与``PyMemoryView_*`` C API一起使用。"

#: ../NEWS:11427
msgid ""
":gh:`114685`: :c:func:`PyObject_GetBuffer` now raises a :exc:`SystemError` "
"if called with :c:macro:`PyBUF_READ` or :c:macro:`PyBUF_WRITE` as flags. "
"These flags should only be used with the ``PyMemoryView_*`` C API."
msgstr ""
":gh:`114685`: 如果 :c:func:`PyObject_GetBuffer` 被调用时使用了 :c:macro:`PyBUF_READ` "
"或 :c:macro:`PyBUF_WRITE` 作为标志，现在会引发 "
":exc:`SystemError`。这些标志应仅与``PyMemoryView_*`` C API一起使用。"

#: ../NEWS:11431
msgid ""
":gh:`114626`: Add ``PyCFunctionFast`` and ``PyCFunctionFastWithKeywords`` "
"typedefs (identical to the existing ``_PyCFunctionFast`` and "
"``_PyCFunctionFastWithKeywords`` typedefs, just without a leading ``_`` "
"prefix)."
msgstr ""
":gh:`114626`: 添加 ``PyCFunctionFast`` 和 ``PyCFunctionFastWithKeywords`` "
"类型定义（与现有的 ``_PyCFunctionFast`` 和 ``_PyCFunctionFastWithKeywords`` "
"类型定义相同，只是没有前导的 ``_`` 前缀）。"

#: ../NEWS:11436
msgid ""
":gh:`114329`: Add :c:func:`PyList_GetItemRef`, which is similar to "
":c:func:`PyList_GetItem` but returns a :term:`strong reference` instead of a"
" :term:`borrowed reference`."
msgstr ""
":gh:`114329`: 添加 :c:func:`PyList_GetItemRef`，它与 :c:func:`PyList_GetItem` "
"类似，但返回的是 :term:`strong reference` 而不是  :term:`borrowed reference`。"

#: ../NEWS:11440
msgid ":gh:`110850`: Add PyTime C API:"
msgstr ":gh:`110850`: 添加 PyTime C API："

#: ../NEWS:11442
msgid ":c:type:`PyTime_t` type."
msgstr ":c:type:`PyTime_t` 类型。"

#: ../NEWS:11443
msgid ":c:var:`PyTime_MIN` and :c:var:`PyTime_MAX` constants."
msgstr ":c:var:`PyTime_MIN` 和 :c:var:`PyTime_MAX` 常量。"

#: ../NEWS:11444
msgid ""
":c:func:`PyTime_AsSecondsDouble`, :c:func:`PyTime_Monotonic`, "
":c:func:`PyTime_PerfCounter`, and :c:func:`PyTime_Time` functions."
msgstr ""
":c:func:`PyTime_AsSecondsDouble`, :c:func:`PyTime_Monotonic`, "
":c:func:`PyTime_PerfCounter`, 和 :c:func:`PyTime_Time` 函数。"

#: ../NEWS:11450
msgid ""
":gh:`112066`: Add :c:func:`PyDict_SetDefaultRef`: insert a key and value "
"into a dictionary if the key is not already present. This is similar to "
":meth:`dict.setdefault`, but returns an integer value indicating if the key "
"was already present. It is also similar to :c:func:`PyDict_SetDefault`, but "
"returns a strong reference instead of a borrowed reference."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112066`: 添加 :c:func:`PyDict_SetDefaultRef`：如果键不存在，则将键和值插入字典中。这与 "
":meth:`dict.setdefault` 类似，但返回一个整数值，指示键是否已经存在。它也与 "
":c:func:`PyDict_SetDefault` 类似，但返回的是强引用而不是借用引用。"

#: ../NEWS:11459
msgid "Python 3.13.0 alpha 3"
msgstr "Python 3.13.0 alpha 3"

#: ../NEWS:11461
msgid "*Release date: 2024-01-17*"
msgstr "*发布日期：2024-01-17*"

#: ../NEWS:11466
msgid ""
":gh:`113659`: Skip ``.pth`` files with names starting with a dot or hidden "
"file attribute."
msgstr ":gh:`113659`: 跳过名称以点开头或具有隐藏文件属性的 ``.pth`` 文件。"

#: ../NEWS:11469
msgid ""
":gh:`112302`: Created a Software Bill-of-Materials document and tooling for "
"tracking dependencies."
msgstr ":gh:`112302`: 创建了一个软件物料清单文档和工具，用于跟踪依赖关系。"

#: ../NEWS:11475
msgid ""
":gh:`107901`: Compiler duplicates basic blocks that have an eval breaker "
"check, no line number, and multiple predecessors."
msgstr ":gh:`107901`: 编译器复制具有评估中断检查、无行号和多个前驱的基本块。"

#: ../NEWS:11478
msgid ""
":gh:`107901`: A jump leaving an exception handler back to normal code no "
"longer checks the eval breaker."
msgstr ":gh:`107901`: 离开异常处理程序跳转回正常代码不再检查评估中断。"

#: ../NEWS:11481
msgid ""
":gh:`113655`: Set the C recursion limit to 4000 on Windows, and 10000 on "
"Linux/OSX. This seems to be near the sweet spot to maintain safety, but not "
"compromise backwards compatibility."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113655`: 在 Windows 上将 C 递归限制设置为 4000，在 Linux/OSX 上设置为 "
"10000。这似乎是在保持安全性和不损害向后兼容性之间的最佳点。"

#: ../NEWS:11485
msgid ""
":gh:`113710`: Add typed stack effects to the interpreter DSL, along with "
"various instruction annotations."
msgstr ":gh:`113710`: 向解释器 DSL 添加类型化堆栈效果，以及各种指令注释。"

#: ../NEWS:11488
msgid ""
":gh:`77046`: On Windows, file descriptors wrapping Windows handles are now "
"created non inheritable by default (:pep:`446`). Patch by Zackery Spytz and "
"Victor Stinner."
msgstr ""
":gh:`77046`: 在 Windows 上，默认情况下，包装 Windows 句柄的文件描述符现在创建为不可继承（:pep:`446`）。由 "
"Zackery Spytz 和 Victor Stinner 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11492
msgid ""
":gh:`113853`: Guarantee that all executors make progress. This then "
"guarantees that tier 2 execution always makes progress."
msgstr ":gh:`113853`: 保证所有执行器都取得进展。这进而保证了第 2 层执行总是取得进展。"

#: ../NEWS:11495
msgid ""
":gh:`113753`: Fix an issue where the finalizer of ``PyAsyncGenASend`` "
"objects might not be called if they were allocated from a free list."
msgstr ":gh:`113753`: 修复了如果 ``PyAsyncGenASend`` 对象是从自由列表分配的，其终结器可能不会被调用的问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11498
msgid ""
":gh:`107901`: Compiler changed so that synthetic jumps which are not at loop"
" end no longer check the eval breaker."
msgstr ":gh:`107901`: 编译器更改，使得不在循环结束位置的合成跳转不再检查 eval breaker。"

#: ../NEWS:11501
msgid ""
":gh:`113703`: Fix a regression in the :mod:`codeop` module that was causing "
"it to incorrectly identify incomplete f-strings. Patch by Pablo Galindo"
msgstr ""
":gh:`113703`: 修复了 :mod:`codeop` 模块中的一个回归问题，该问题导致它错误地识别不完整的 f-strings。由 Pablo"
" Galindo 提供补丁"

#: ../NEWS:11504
msgid ""
":gh:`89811`: Check for a valid ``tp_version_tag`` before performing bytecode"
" specializations that rely on this value being usable."
msgstr ":gh:`89811`: 在执行依赖于此值可用的字节码特殊化之前，检查有效的 ``tp_version_tag``。"

#: ../NEWS:11507
msgid ""
":gh:`111488`: Changed error message in case of no 'in' keyword after 'for' "
"in list comprehensions"
msgstr ":gh:`111488`: 更改了列表推导式中 'for' 后没有 'in' 关键字时的错误消息。"

#: ../NEWS:11510
msgid ""
":gh:`113657`: Fix an issue that caused important instruction pointer updates"
" to be optimized out of tier two traces."
msgstr ":gh:`113657`: 修复了一个导致重要指令指针更新在二级跟踪中被优化掉的问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11513
msgid ""
":gh:`113603`: Fixed bug where a redundant NOP is not removed, causing an "
"assertion to fail in the compiler in debug mode."
msgstr ":gh:`113603`: 修复了一个在调试模式下导致编译器断言失败的冗余 NOP 未被移除的错误。"

#: ../NEWS:11516
msgid ""
":gh:`113602`: Fix an error that was causing the parser to try to overwrite "
"existing errors and crashing in the process. Patch by Pablo Galindo"
msgstr ":gh:`113602`: 修复了一个导致解析器尝试覆盖现有错误并在过程中崩溃的错误。由 Pablo Galindo 提供补丁"

#: ../NEWS:11519
msgid ""
":gh:`113486`: No longer issue spurious ``PY_UNWIND`` events for optimized "
"calls to classes."
msgstr ":gh:`113486`: 不再为优化后的类调用发出虚假的 ``PY_UNWIND`` 事件。"

#: ../NEWS:11522
msgid ""
":gh:`113297`: Fix segfault in the compiler on with statement with 19 context"
" managers."
msgstr ":gh:`113297`: 修复了编译器在使用 19 个上下文管理器的 with 语句时出现的段错误。"

#: ../NEWS:11525
msgid ":gh:`113212`: Improve :py:class:`super` error messages."
msgstr ":gh:`113212`: 改进了 :py:class:`super` 的错误消息。"

#: ../NEWS:11527
msgid ""
":gh:`111375`: Only use ``NULL`` in the exception stack to indicate an "
"exception was handled. Patch by Carey Metcalfe."
msgstr ":gh:`111375`: 仅在异常堆栈中使用 ``NULL`` 来表示异常已被处理。由 Carey Metcalfe 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11530
msgid ""
":gh:`112215`: Increase the C recursion limit by a factor of 3 for non-debug "
"builds, except for webassembly and s390 platforms which are unchanged. This "
"mitigates some regressions in 3.12 with deep recursion mixing builtin (C) "
"and Python code."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112215`: 对于非调试构建，将 C 递归限制增加了 3 倍，但 webassembly 和 s390 平台保持不变。这缓解了 3.12 "
"中混合内置（C）和 Python 代码的深度递归的一些回归问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11535
msgid ""
":gh:`113054`: Fixed bug where a redundant NOP is not removed, causing an "
"assertion to fail in the compiler in debug mode."
msgstr ":gh:`113054`: 修复了一个在调试模式下导致编译器断言失败的冗余 NOP 未被移除的错误。"

#: ../NEWS:11538
msgid ""
":gh:`106905`: Use per AST-parser state rather than global state to track "
"recursion depth within the AST parser to prevent potential race condition "
"due to simultaneous parsing."
msgstr ""
":gh:`106905`: 使用每个 AST 解析器状态而非全局状态来跟踪 AST 解析器内的递归深度，以防止由于同时解析而导致的潜在竞争条件。"

#: ../NEWS:11542
msgid ""
"The issue primarily showed up in 3.11 by multithreaded users of "
":func:`ast.parse`.  In 3.12 a change to when garbage collection can be "
"triggered prevented the race condition from occurring."
msgstr ""
"该问题主要在3.11版本中由 :func:`ast.parse` 的多线程用户发现。在3.12版本中，对垃圾回收触发时机的更改防止了竞态条件的发生。"

#: ../NEWS:11546
msgid ""
":gh:`108866`: Change the API and contract of ``_PyExecutorObject`` to return"
" the next_instr pointer, instead of the frame, and to always execute at "
"least one instruction."
msgstr ""
":gh:`108866`: 更改 ``_PyExecutorObject`` "
"的API和契约，使其返回next_instr指针而非帧，并确保至少执行一条指令。"

#: ../NEWS:11550
msgid ":gh:`90350`: Optimize builtin functions :func:`min` and :func:`max`."
msgstr ":gh:`90350`: 优化内置函数 :func:`min` 和 :func:`max`。"

#: ../NEWS:11552
msgid ""
":gh:`112943`: Correctly compute end column offsets for multiline tokens in "
"the :mod:`tokenize` module. Patch by Pablo Galindo"
msgstr ":gh:`112943`: 在 :mod:`tokenize` 模块中正确计算多行令牌的结束列偏移。补丁由Pablo Galindo提供。"

#: ../NEWS:11555
msgid ""
":gh:`112125`: Fix ``None.__ne__(None)`` returning ``NotImplemented`` instead"
" of ``False``."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112125`: 修复 ``None.__ne__(None)``返回 ``NotImplemented`` 而非 ``False`` "
"的问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11558
msgid ""
":gh:`74616`: :func:`input` now raises a ValueError when output on the "
"terminal if the prompt contains embedded null characters instead of silently"
" truncating it."
msgstr ""
":gh:`74616`: 当提示包含嵌入的null字符时，:func:`input` 现在会在终端输出时引发ValueError，而不是静默截断。"

#: ../NEWS:11562
msgid ""
":gh:`112716`: Fix SystemError in the ``import`` statement and in "
"``__reduce__()`` methods of builtin types when ``__builtins__`` is not a "
"dict."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112716`: 修复当 ``__builtins__`` 不是字典时，``import`` 语句和内置类型的 "
"``__reduce__()``方法中的SystemError。"

#: ../NEWS:11566
msgid ""
":gh:`112730`: Use color to highlight error locations in tracebacks. Patch by"
" Pablo Galindo"
msgstr ":gh:`112730`: 使用颜色高亮tracebacks中的错误位置。由Pablo Galindo提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11569
msgid ""
":gh:`112625`: Fixes a bug where a bytearray object could be cleared while "
"iterating over an argument in the ``bytearray.join()`` method that could "
"result in reading memory after it was freed."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112625`: 修复在 ``bytearray.join()`` "
"方法中迭代参数时可能会清除bytearray对象，导致读取已释放内存的bug。"

#: ../NEWS:11573
msgid ""
":gh:`112660`: Do not clear unexpected errors during formatting error "
"messages for ImportError and AttributeError for modules."
msgstr ":gh:`112660`: 在格式化模块的ImportError和AttributeError错误消息时，不清除意外错误。"

#: ../NEWS:11576
msgid ""
":gh:`105967`: Workaround a bug in Apple's macOS platform zlib library where "
":func:`zlib.crc32` and :func:`binascii.crc32` could produce incorrect "
"results on multi-gigabyte inputs. Including when using :mod:`zipfile` on "
"zips containing large data."
msgstr ""
":gh:`105967`: 解决Apple的macOS平台zlib库中的一个bug，其中 :func:`zlib.crc32` 和 "
":func:`binascii.crc32` 在多GB输入上可能产生不正确的结果。包括在使用 :mod:`zipfile` "
"处理包含大数据的zip文件时。"

#: ../NEWS:11581
msgid ""
":gh:`95754`: Provide a better error message when accessing invalid "
"attributes on partially initialized modules. The origin of the module being "
"accessed is now included in the message to help with the common issue of "
"shadowing other modules."
msgstr ""
":gh:`95754`: 在访问部分初始化模块上的无效属性时提供更好的错误消息。现在消息中包含了被访问模块的来源，以帮助解决模块遮蔽其他模块的常见问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11586
msgid ""
":gh:`112217`: Add check for the type of ``__cause__`` returned from calling "
"the type ``T`` in ``raise from T``."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112217`: 添加对 ``raise from T``中调用类型 ``T`` 返回的 ``__cause__`` 类型的检查。"

#: ../NEWS:11589
msgid ""
":gh:`111058`: Change coro.cr_frame/gen.gi_frame to return ``None`` after the"
" coroutine/generator has been closed. This fixes a bug where "
":func:`~inspect.getcoroutinestate` and :func:`~inspect.getgeneratorstate` "
"return the wrong state for a closed coroutine/generator."
msgstr ""
":gh:`111058`: 修改 coro.cr_frame/gen.gi_frame 在协程/生成器关闭后返回 ``None``。这修复了 "
":func:`~inspect.getcoroutinestate` 和 :func:`~inspect.getgeneratorstate` "
"对于已关闭协程/生成器返回错误状态的 bug。"

#: ../NEWS:11594
msgid ""
":gh:`112388`: Fix an error that was causing the parser to try to overwrite "
"tokenizer errors. Patch by pablo Galindo"
msgstr ":gh:`112388`: 修复导致解析器尝试覆盖 tokenizer 错误的错误。由 Pablo Galindo 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11597
msgid ""
":gh:`112387`: Fix error positions for decoded strings with backwards "
"tokenize errors. Patch by Pablo Galindo"
msgstr ":gh:`112387`: 修复解码字符串中反向 tokenize 错误的错误位置。由 Pablo Galindo 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11600
msgid ""
":gh:`99606`: Make code generated for an empty f-string identical to the code"
" of an empty normal string."
msgstr ":gh:`99606`: 使空 f-string 生成的代码与空普通字符串的代码相同。"

#: ../NEWS:11603
msgid ""
":gh:`112367`: Avoid undefined behaviour when using the perf trampolines by "
"not freeing the code arenas until shutdown. Patch by Pablo Galindo"
msgstr ""
":gh:`112367`: 通过不释放代码区域直到关闭，避免使用 perf trampolines 时的未定义行为。补丁由 Pablo Galindo "
"提供。"

#: ../NEWS:11606
msgid ""
":gh:`112320`: The Tier 2 translator now tracks the confidence level for "
"staying \"on trace\" (i.e. not exiting back to the Tier 1 interpreter) for "
"branch instructions based on the number of bits set in the branch "
"\"counter\". Trace translation ends when the confidence drops below 1/3rd."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112320`: Tier 2 翻译器现在基于分支“计数器”中设置的位数跟踪保持“在跟踪上”（即不退回到 Tier 1 "
"解释器）的置信水平。当置信度低于 1/3 时，跟踪翻译结束。"

#: ../NEWS:11611
msgid ""
":gh:`109598`: "
":c:func:`PyComplex_RealAsDouble`/:c:func:`PyComplex_ImagAsDouble` now tries "
"to convert an object to a :class:`complex` instance using its "
"``__complex__()`` method before falling back to the ``__float__()`` method. "
"Patch by Sergey B Kirpichev."
msgstr ""
":gh:`109598`: "
":c:func:`PyComplex_RealAsDouble`/:c:func:`PyComplex_ImagAsDouble` 现在尝试使用对象的 "
"``__complex__()`` 方法将其转换为 :class:`complex` 实例，然后再回退到 ``__float__()`` 方法。由 "
"Sergey B Kirpichev 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11617
msgid ""
":gh:`94606`: Fix UnicodeEncodeError when :func:`email.message.get_payload` "
"reads a message with a Unicode surrogate character and the message content "
"is not well-formed for surrogateescape encoding. Patch by Sidney Markowitz."
msgstr ""
":gh:`94606`: 修复当 :func:`email.message.get_payload` 读取含有 Unicode 代理字符且消息内容不适合"
" surrogateescape 编码的消息时的 UnicodeEncodeError。由 Sidney Markowitz 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11622
msgid ""
":issue:`21861`: Use the object's actual class name in "
":meth:`!_io.FileIO.__repr__`, :meth:`!_io._WindowsConsoleIO` and "
":meth:`!_io.TextIOWrapper.__repr__`, to make these methods subclass "
"friendly."
msgstr ""
":issue:`21861`: 在 :meth:`!_io.FileIO.__repr__`, "
":meth:`!_io._WindowsConsoleIO` 和 :meth:`!_io.TextIOWrapper.__repr__` "
"中使用对象的实际类名，使这些方法对子类友好。"

#: ../NEWS:11627
msgid ":issue:`45369`: Remove LibreSSL workarounds as per :pep:`644`."
msgstr ":issue:`45369`: 根据 :pep:`644` 移除 LibreSSL 的变通方法。"

#: ../NEWS:11629
msgid ":issue:`34392`: Added :func:`sys._is_interned`."
msgstr ":issue:`34392`: 添加 :func:`sys._is_interned`。"

#: ../NEWS:11634
msgid ""
":gh:`114077`: Fix possible :exc:`OverflowError` in "
":meth:`socket.socket.sendfile` when pass *count* larger than 2 GiB on 32-bit"
" platform."
msgstr ""
":gh:`114077`: 修复在 32 位平台上传递大于 2 GiB 的 *count* 时 "
":meth:`socket.socket.sendfile` 中可能出现的 :exc:`OverflowError`。"

#: ../NEWS:11638
msgid ""
":gh:`111803`: :mod:`plistlib` now supports loading more deeply nested lists "
"in binary format."
msgstr ":gh:`111803`: :mod:`plistlib` 现在支持以二进制格式加载更深层次的嵌套列表。"

#: ../NEWS:11641
msgid ""
":gh:`114014`: Fixed a bug in :class:`fractions.Fraction` where an invalid "
"string using ``d`` in the decimals part creates a different error compared "
"to other invalid letters/characters. Patch by Jeremiah Gabriel Pascual."
msgstr ""
":gh:`114014`: 修复了 :class:`fractions.Fraction` 中的一个 bug，该 bug 在使用 ``d`` "
"作为小数部分的无效字符串时，会生成与其他无效字母/字符不同的错误。由 Jeremiah Gabriel Pascual 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11645
msgid ""
":gh:`108364`: :meth:`sqlite3.Connection.iterdump` now ensures that foreign "
"key support is disabled before dumping the database schema, if there is any "
"foreign key violation. Patch by Erlend E. Aasland and Mariusz Felisiak."
msgstr ""
":gh:`108364`: :meth:`sqlite3.Connection.iterdump` "
"现在确保在转储数据库模式之前禁用外键支持，如果有任何外键违规。由 Erlend E. Aasland 和 Mariusz Felisiak 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11650
msgid ""
":gh:`113971`: The :class:`zipfile.ZipInfo` previously protected "
"``._compresslevel`` attribute has been made public as ``.compress_level`` "
"with the old ``_compresslevel`` name remaining available as a property to "
"retain compatibility."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113971`: :class:`zipfile.ZipInfo` 之前受保护的 ``._compresslevel`` 属性现在公开为 "
"``.compress_level``，旧的 ``_compresslevel`` 名称仍作为属性保留以保持兼容性。"

#: ../NEWS:11655
msgid ""
":gh:`113877`: Fix :mod:`tkinter` method ``winfo_pathname()`` on 64-bit "
"Windows."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113877`: 修复 64 位 Windows 上的 :mod:`tkinter` 方法 ``winfo_pathname()``。"

#: ../NEWS:11658
msgid ""
":gh:`113868`: Added :data:`mmap.MAP_NORESERVE`, :data:`mmap.MAP_NOEXTEND`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_HASSEMAPHORE`, :data:`mmap.MAP_NOCACHE`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_JIT`, :data:`mmap.MAP_RESILIENT_CODESIGN`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_RESILIENT_MEDIA`, :data:`mmap.MAP_32BIT`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_TRANSLATED_ALLOW_EXECUTE`, :data:`mmap.MAP_UNIX03` and "
":data:`mmap.MAP_TPRO`. All of them are ``mmap(2)`` flags on macOS."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113868`: 添加了 :data:`mmap.MAP_NORESERVE`, :data:`mmap.MAP_NOEXTEND`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_HASSEMAPHORE`, :data:`mmap.MAP_NOCACHE`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_JIT`, :data:`mmap.MAP_RESILIENT_CODESIGN`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_RESILIENT_MEDIA`, :data:`mmap.MAP_32BIT`, "
":data:`mmap.MAP_TRANSLATED_ALLOW_EXECUTE`, :data:`mmap.MAP_UNIX03` 和 "
":data:`mmap.MAP_TPRO`。这些都是 macOS 上的 ``mmap(2)`` 标志。"

#: ../NEWS:11665
msgid ""
":gh:`113848`: :func:`asyncio.TaskGroup` and :func:`asyncio.timeout` context "
"managers now handle :exc:`~asyncio.CancelledError` subclasses as well as "
"exact :exc:`!CancelledError`."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113848`: :func:`asyncio.TaskGroup` 和 :func:`asyncio.timeout` "
"上下文管理器现在也处理 :exc:`~asyncio.CancelledError` 子类以及确切的 :exc:`!CancelledError`。"

#: ../NEWS:11669
msgid ""
":gh:`113661`: unittest runner: Don't exit 5 if tests were skipped. The "
"intention of exiting 5 was to detect issues where the test suite wasn't "
"discovered at all. If we skipped tests, it was correctly discovered."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113661`: unittest 运行器：如果测试被跳过，不要退出 5。退出 5 "
"的意图是检测测试套件根本没有被发现的问题。如果我们跳过了测试，那么它已经被正确发现了。"

#: ../NEWS:11673
msgid ""
":gh:`96037`: Insert :exc:`TimeoutError` in the context of the exception that"
" was raised during exiting an expired :func:`asyncio.timeout` block."
msgstr ""
":gh:`96037`: 在退出过期的 :func:`asyncio.timeout` 块期间引发的异常的上下文中插入 "
":exc:`TimeoutError`。"

#: ../NEWS:11676
msgid ""
":gh:`113781`: Silence unraisable AttributeError when warnings are emitted "
"during Python finalization."
msgstr ":gh:`113781`: 在 Python 结束期间发出警告时，静默不可引发的 AttributeError。"

#: ../NEWS:11679
msgid ""
":gh:`113238`: Add ``Anchor`` to ``importlib.resources`` (in order for the "
"code to comply with the documentation)"
msgstr ":gh:`113238`: 向 ``importlib.resources`` 添加 ``Anchor`` (为了使代码符合文档) 。"

#: ../NEWS:11682
msgid ""
":gh:`111693`: :func:`asyncio.Condition.wait` now re-raises the same "
":exc:`CancelledError` instance that may have caused it to be interrupted. "
"Fixed race condition in :func:`asyncio.Semaphore.acquire` when interrupted "
"with a :exc:`CancelledError`."
msgstr ""
":gh:`111693`: :func:`asyncio.Condition.wait` 现在会重新抛出可能导致其被中断的同一个 "
":exc:`CancelledError` 实例。修复了在 :func:`asyncio.Semaphore.acquire` 被 "
":exc:`CancelledError` 中断时的竞态条件。"

#: ../NEWS:11687
msgid ""
":gh:`113791`: Add ``CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW_APPROX`` and "
"``CLOCK_UPTIME_RAW_APPROX`` to :mod:`time` on macOS. These are clocks "
"available on macOS 10.12 or later."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113791`: 在 macOS 上向 :mod:`time` 添加 ``CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW_APPROX`` 和 "
"``CLOCK_UPTIME_RAW_APPROX``。这些时钟在 macOS 10.12 或更高版本上可用。"

#: ../NEWS:11691
msgid ""
":gh:`112932`: Restore the ability for :mod:`zipfile` to ``extractall`` from "
"zip files with a \"/\" directory entry in them as is commonly added to zips "
"by some wiki or bug tracker data exporters."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112932`: 恢复 :mod:`zipfile` 从含有 \"/\" 目录条目的 zip 文件中 ``extractall`` "
"的能力，这是某些 wiki 或 bug 跟踪器数据导出器常见添加到 zip 文件中的情况。"

#: ../NEWS:11695
msgid ""
":gh:`113568`: Raise deprecation warnings from :class:`pathlib.PurePath` and "
"not its private base class ``PurePathBase``."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113568`: 从 :class:`pathlib.PurePath` 而不是其私有基类 ``PurePathBase`` 中引发弃用警告。"

#: ../NEWS:11698
msgid ""
":gh:`113594`: Fix :exc:`UnicodeEncodeError` in :mod:`email` when re-fold "
"lines that contain unknown-8bit encoded part followed by non-unknown-8bit "
"encoded part."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113594`: 修复 :mod:`email` 中当重新折叠包含 unknown-8bit 编码部分后跟非 unknown-8bit "
"编码部分的行时引发的 :exc:`UnicodeEncodeError`。"

#: ../NEWS:11702
msgid ""
":gh:`113538`: In :meth:`asyncio.StreamReaderProtocol.connection_made`, there"
" is callback that logs an error if the task wrapping the \"connected "
"callback\" fails. This callback would itself fail if the task was cancelled."
" Prevent this by checking whether the task was cancelled first. If so, close"
" the transport but don't log an error."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113538`: 在 :meth:`asyncio.StreamReaderProtocol.connection_made` "
"中，有一个回调函数，如果包装“连接回调”的任务失败，则会记录错误。如果任务被取消，这个回调本身会失败。通过首先检查任务是否被取消来防止这种情况。如果是，关闭传输但不记录错误。"

#: ../NEWS:11708
msgid ""
":gh:`113626`: Add support for the *allow_code* argument in the "
":mod:`marshal` module. Passing ``allow_code=False`` prevents serialization "
"and de-serialization of code objects which is incompatible between Python "
"versions."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113626`: 在 :mod:`marshal` 模块中添加对 *allow_code* 参数的支持。传递 "
"``allow_code=False`` 可以防止代码对象的序列化和反序列化，这在 Python 版本之间是不兼容的。"

#: ../NEWS:11713
msgid ""
":gh:`85567`: Fix resource warnings for unclosed files in :mod:`pickle` and "
":mod:`pickletools` command line interfaces."
msgstr ":gh:`85567`: 修复 :mod:`pickle` 和 :mod:`pickletools` 命令行界面中未关闭文件的资源警告。"

#: ../NEWS:11716
msgid ":gh:`113537`: Support loads ``str`` in :func:`plistlib.loads`."
msgstr ":gh:`113537`: 在 :func:`plistlib.loads` 中支持加载 ``str``。"

#: ../NEWS:11718
msgid ""
":gh:`89850`: Add default implementations of "
":meth:`pickle.Pickler.persistent_id` and "
":meth:`pickle.Unpickler.persistent_load` methods in the C implementation. "
"Calling ``super().persistent_id()`` and ``super().persistent_load()`` in "
"subclasses of the C implementation of :class:`pickle.Pickler` and "
":class:`pickle.Unpickler` classes no longer causes infinite recursion."
msgstr ""
":gh:`89850`: 在 C 实现中添加 :meth:`pickle.Pickler.persistent_id` 和 "
":meth:`pickle.Unpickler.persistent_load` 方法的默认实现。在 :class:`pickle.Pickler` 和"
" :class:`pickle.Unpickler` 类的 C 实现的子类中调用 ``super().persistent_id()`` 和 "
"``super().persistent_load()`` 不再导致无限递归。"

#: ../NEWS:11725
msgid ""
":gh:`113569`: Indicate if there were no actual calls in unittest "
":meth:`~unittest.mock.Mock.assert_has_calls` failure."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113569`: 在 unittest 的 :meth:`~unittest.mock.Mock.assert_has_calls` "
"失败时，如果实际上没有调用，进行指示。"

#: ../NEWS:11728
msgid ""
":gh:`101225`: Increase the backlog for "
":class:`multiprocessing.connection.Listener` objects created by "
":mod:`multiprocessing.manager` and :mod:`multiprocessing.resource_sharer` to"
" significantly reduce the risk of getting a connection refused error when "
"creating a :class:`multiprocessing.connection.Connection` to them."
msgstr ""
":gh:`101225`: 增加由 :mod:`multiprocessing.manager` 和 "
":mod:`multiprocessing.resource_sharer` 创建的 "
":class:`multiprocessing.connection.Listener` 对象的积压，以显著降低在创建到它们的 "
":class:`multiprocessing.connection.Connection` 时遇到连接拒绝错误的风险。"

#: ../NEWS:11734
msgid ""
":gh:`113568`: Raise audit events from :class:`pathlib.Path` and not its "
"private base class ``PathBase``."
msgstr ":gh:`113568`: 从 :class:`pathlib.Path` 而不是其私有基类 ``PathBase`` 引发审计事件。"

#: ../NEWS:11737
msgid ""
":gh:`113543`: Make sure that ``webbrowser.MacOSXOSAScript`` sends "
"``webbrowser.open`` audit event."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113543`: 确保 ``webbrowser.MacOSXOSAScript`` 发送 ``webbrowser.open`` 审计事件。"

#: ../NEWS:11740
msgid ""
":gh:`113028`: When a second reference to a string appears in the input to "
":mod:`pickle`, and the Python implementation is in use, we are guaranteed "
"that a single copy gets pickled and a single object is shared when reloaded."
" Previously, in protocol 0, when a string contained certain characters (e.g."
" newline) it resulted in duplicate objects."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113028`: 当字符串的第二个引用出现在 :mod:`pickle` 的输入中，并且使用 Python 实现时，我们保证只有一个副本被 "
"pickle，并且在重新加载时共享一个对象。以前，在协议 0 中，当字符串包含某些字符（如换行符）时，会导致对象重复。"

#: ../NEWS:11746
msgid ":gh:`113421`: Fix multiprocessing logger for ``%(filename)s``."
msgstr ":gh:`113421`: 修复多进程日志记录器对于 ``%(filename)s`` 的问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11748
msgid ""
":gh:`111784`: Fix segfaults in the ``_elementtree`` module. Fix first "
"segfault during deallocation of ``_elementtree.XMLParser`` instances by "
"keeping strong reference to ``pyexpat`` module in module state for capsule "
"lifetime. Fix second segfault which happens in the same deallocation process"
"  by keeping strong reference to ``_elementtree`` module in ``XMLParser`` "
"structure for ``_elementtree`` module lifetime."
msgstr ""
":gh:`111784`: 修复 ``_elementtree`` 模块中的段错误。通过在模块状态中为胶囊生命周期保持对 ``pyexpat`` "
"模块的强引用，修复在 ``_elementtree.XMLParser`` 实例的释放过程中第一次出现的段错误。通过在 ``XMLParser`` "
"结构中为 ``_elementtree`` 模块生命周期保持对 ``_elementtree`` 模块的强引用，修复在同一释放过程中第二次出现的段错误。"

#: ../NEWS:11755
msgid ""
":gh:`113407`: Fix import of :mod:`unittest.mock` when CPython is built "
"without docstrings."
msgstr ":gh:`113407`: 修复当 CPython 构建时没有文档字符串时导入 :mod:`unittest.mock` 的问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11758
msgid ""
":gh:`113320`: Fix regression in Python 3.12 where :class:`~typing.Protocol` "
"classes that were not marked as :func:`runtime-checkable "
"<typing.runtime_checkable>` would be unnecessarily introspected, potentially"
" causing exceptions to be raised if the protocol had problematic members. "
"Patch by Alex Waygood."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113320`: 修复 Python 3.12 中的一个回归问题，其中未标记为 :func:`runtime-checkable "
"<typing.runtime_checkable>` 的 :class:`~typing.Protocol` "
"类会被不必要地内省，如果协议有问题的成员，可能会导致异常被引发。由 Alex Waygood 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11764
msgid ""
":gh:`53502`: Add a new option ``aware_datetime`` in :mod:`plistlib` to loads"
" or dumps aware datetime."
msgstr ""
":gh:`53502`: 在 :mod:`plistlib` 中添加一个新选项 ``aware_datetime`` 以加载或转储感知日期时间。"

#: ../NEWS:11767
msgid ""
":gh:`113358`: Fix rendering tracebacks with exceptions with a broken "
"__getattr__"
msgstr ":gh:`113358`: 修复了当异常具有损坏的 __getattr__ 时渲染回溯的问题。"

#: ../NEWS:11770
msgid ""
":gh:`113214`: Fix an ``AttributeError`` during asyncio SSL protocol aborts "
"in SSL-over-SSL scenarios."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113214`: 修复了在 SSL-over-SSL 场景中 asyncio SSL 协议中止时出现的 ``AttributeError``。"

#: ../NEWS:11773
msgid ":gh:`113246`: Update bundled pip to 23.3.2."
msgstr ":gh:`113246`: 更新捆绑的 pip 到 23.3.2 版本。"

#: ../NEWS:11775
msgid ":gh:`87264`: Fixed tarfile list() method to show file type."
msgstr ":gh:`87264`: 修复了 tarfile list() 方法以显示文件类型。"

#: ../NEWS:11777
msgid ""
":gh:`112182`: :meth:`asyncio.futures.Future.set_exception` now transforms "
":exc:`StopIteration` into :exc:`RuntimeError` instead of hanging or other "
"misbehavior. Patch contributed by Jamie Phan."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112182`: :meth:`asyncio.futures.Future.set_exception` 现在将 "
":exc:`StopIteration` 转换为 :exc:`RuntimeError`，而不是挂起或其他异常行为。由 Jamie Phan 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11781
msgid ""
":gh:`113225`: Speed up :meth:`pathlib.Path.glob` by using "
":attr:`os.DirEntry.path` where possible."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113225`: 通过尽可能使用 :attr:`os.DirEntry.path` 来加速 "
":meth:`pathlib.Path.glob`。"

#: ../NEWS:11784
msgid ""
":gh:`113149`: Improve error message when a JSON array or object contains a "
"trailing comma. Patch by Carson Radtke."
msgstr ":gh:`113149`: 当 JSON 数组或对象包含尾随逗号时，改进了错误消息。补丁由 Carson Radtke 提供。"

#: ../NEWS:11787
msgid ""
":gh:`113117`: The :mod:`subprocess` module can now use the "
":func:`os.posix_spawn` function with ``close_fds=True`` on platforms where "
"``posix_spawn_file_actions_addclosefrom_np`` is available. Patch by Jakub "
"Kulik."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113117`: :mod:`subprocess` 模块现在可以在支持 "
"``posix_spawn_file_actions_addclosefrom_np`` 的平台上使用 :func:`os.posix_spawn` "
"函数和 ``close_fds=True``。由 Jakub Kulik 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11792
msgid ""
":gh:`113199`: Make ``http.client.HTTPResponse.read1`` and "
"``http.client.HTTPResponse.readline`` close IO after reading all data when "
"content length is known. Patch by Illia Volochii."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113199`: 使得 ``http.client.HTTPResponse.read1`` 和 "
"``http.client.HTTPResponse.readline`` 在知道内容长度时读取所有数据后关闭 IO。由 Illia Volochii "
"提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11796
msgid ""
":gh:`113191`: Add support of :func:`os.fchmod` and a file descriptor in "
":func:`os.chmod` on Windows."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113191`: 在 Windows 上添加对 :func:`os.fchmod` 和文件描述符在 :func:`os.chmod` "
"中的支持。"

#: ../NEWS:11799
msgid ""
":gh:`113188`: Fix :func:`shutil.copymode` and :func:`shutil.copystat` on "
"Windows. Previously they worked differently if *dst* is a symbolic link: "
"they modified the permission bits of *dst* itself rather than the file it "
"points to if *follow_symlinks* is true or *src* is not a symbolic link, and "
"did not modify the permission bits if *follow_symlinks* is false and *src* "
"is a symbolic link."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113188`: 修复了 Windows 上的 :func:`shutil.copymode` 和 "
":func:`shutil.copystat`。之前，如果 *dst* 是一个符号链接，它们的行为会有所不同：如果 *follow_symlinks* "
"为真或 *src* 不是符号链接，它们会修改 *dst* 本身的权限位而不是它指向的文件；如果 *follow_symlinks* 为假且 *src* "
"是符号链接，则不会修改权限位。"

#: ../NEWS:11806
msgid ""
":gh:`113119`: :func:`os.posix_spawn` now accepts ``env=None``, which makes "
"the newly spawned process use the current process environment. Patch by "
"Jakub Kulik."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113119`: :func:`os.posix_spawn` 现在接受 ``env=None``，这使得新生成的进程使用当前进程环境。由 "
"Jakub Kulik 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11810
msgid ""
":gh:`113202`: Add a ``strict`` option to ``batched()`` in the ``itertools`` "
"module."
msgstr ":gh:`113202`: 在 ``itertools`` 模块中的 ``batched()`` 添加了一个 ``strict`` 选项。"

#: ../NEWS:11813
msgid ":gh:`61648`: Detect line numbers of properties in doctests."
msgstr ":gh:`61648`: 检测 doctests 中属性的行号。"

#: ../NEWS:11815
msgid ""
":gh:`113175`: Sync with importlib_metadata 7.0, including improved type "
"annotations, fixed issue with symlinked packages in "
"``package_distributions``, added ``EntryPoints.__repr__``, introduced the "
"``diagnose`` script, added ``Distribution.origin`` property, and removed "
"deprecated ``EntryPoint`` access by numeric index (tuple behavior)."
msgstr ""
":gh:`113175`: 与 importlib_metadata 7.0 同步，包括改进的类型注释，修复了 "
"``package_distributions`` 中符号链接包的问题，添加了 ``EntryPoints.__repr__``，引入了 "
"``diagnose`` 脚本，添加了 ``Distribution.origin`` 属性，并移除了通过数字索引（元组行为）访问已弃用的 "
"``EntryPoint``。"

#: ../NEWS:11821
msgid ""
":gh:`59616`: Add support of :func:`os.lchmod` and the *follow_symlinks* "
"argument in :func:`os.chmod` on Windows. Note that the default value of "
"*follow_symlinks* in :func:`!os.lchmod` is ``False`` on Windows."
msgstr ""
":gh:`59616`: 在 Windows 上添加了对 :func:`os.lchmod` 和 :func:`os.chmod` 中 "
"*follow_symlinks* 参数的支持。注意，在 Windows 上 :func:`!os.lchmod` 的 "
"*follow_symlinks* 默认值为 ``False``。"

#: ../NEWS:11825
msgid ""
":gh:`112559`: :func:`signal.signal` and :func:`signal.getsignal` no longer "
"call ``repr`` on callable handlers. :func:`asyncio.run` and "
":meth:`asyncio.Runner.run` no longer call ``repr`` on the task results. "
"Patch by Yilei Yang."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112559`: :func:`signal.signal` 和 :func:`signal.getsignal` 不再对可调用的处理器调用 "
"``repr``。:func:`asyncio.run` 和 :meth:`asyncio.Runner.run` 不再对任务结果调用 "
"``repr``。由 Yilei Yang 提供补丁。"

#: ../NEWS:11830
msgid ""
":gh:`112962`: :mod:`dis` module functions add cache information to the "
":class:`~dis.Instruction` instance rather than creating fake "
":class:`~dis.Instruction` instances to represent the cache entries."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112962`: :mod:`dis` 模块函数将缓存信息添加到 :class:`~dis.Instruction` 实例中，而不是创建假的 "
":class:`~dis.Instruction` 实例来表示缓存条目。"

#: ../NEWS:11834
msgid ""
":gh:`112989`: Reduce overhead to connect sockets with :mod:`asyncio` "
"SelectorEventLoop."
msgstr ":gh:`112989`: 减少了使用 :mod:`asyncio` SelectorEventLoop 连接套接字的开销。"

#: ../NEWS:11837
msgid ""
":gh:`112970`: Use :c:func:`!closefrom` on Linux where available (e.g. "
"glibc-2.34), rather than only FreeBSD."
msgstr ""
":gh:`112970`: 在 Linux 上可用时（如 glibc-2.34）使用 :c:func:`!closefrom`，而不仅限于 "
"FreeBSD。"

#: ../NEWS:11840
msgid ""
":gh:`110190`: Fix ctypes structs with array on PPC64LE platform by setting "
